Upstream: https://github.com/anthropics/skills, path skills/docx
Pinned commit: e4bb5d960d87126ff3b3a8af1a104b7db67560ba
License: Apache-2.0 (LICENSE.txt in this folder, copied unchanged from upstream)

Modified by TOFI: only the editing half of the upstream Skill is kept (the
upstream docx-js creation path belongs to the document-report Skill here). The
SKILL.md text was rewritten for the TOFI Bot computer. The upstream scripts
were replaced by one script, scripts/docx_edit.py, that follows the ideas of
comment.py (comment parts, relationships and anchors), merge_runs.py (text that
Word splits over runs must stay findable), accept_changes.py (accepting tracked
changes, here done in XML without a LibreOffice macro) and
office/validators/redlining.py (every text change must be tracked) with these
changes: no XSD schema bundle and no defusedxml (lxml with entity resolution
and network access off); no LD_PRELOAD socket shim and no compiled code; no
in-place editing and no auto-repair (every command writes a new file and fails
loudly); tracked replacement and rejection of tracked changes were added; the
long XML material moved to references/xml.md.
